.TH CLEANPKG 1 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cleanpkg \- clean retained failed build state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cleanpkg
.IR PACKAGE ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cleanpkg
removes failed
.IR /build/PACKAGE.buildpkg
workspaces through the trusted lifecycle: the workspace must exist
as a real directory inside the build root and carry the exact
marker content
.IR saphira-buildpkg-failed/v1 ;
anything else (unmarked workspaces, non-directories, symlinks,
paths outside the build root, wrong markers) is refused, never
blessed or overwritten.
.PP
A retained overlay holder is terminated first, but only after its
recorded pid is verified against the holder marker and its live
cmdline still names this workspace: recycled or unrelated pids are
never killed. Vanished pids are silent. The whole operation runs
unprivileged; cleanpkg never escalates and must stay non-root.
.SH OPTIONS
This command takes no options beyond the package names.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /build/PACKAGE.buildpkg/FAILED
The trusted failure marker gate.
.TP
.I /build/PACKAGE.buildpkg/overlay-holder.json
Recorded holder identity for verified termination.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Removed (or nothing to do for a missing workspace).
.TP
.B 1
Refusal (unmarked, untrusted marker, outside root, invalid name) or
a mount that will not release.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
cleanpkg nginx
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recipe (5),
.BR saphira (7),
.BR buildpkg (1),
.BR resolvepkg (1),
.BR saphira-build (8)
